      "id": "s03",
      "duration": 25.678367,
      "text": "Weight is gravity, pulling the object vertically down. Its size is mass times gravity. For Cambridge paper 4, use g equals 10 meters per second squared. The bench pushes back with a normal reaction. Normal means perpendicular to the surface. Tilt the surface and the reaction tilts too. Weight still points straight down.",
