    {
      "id": "s09",
      "duration": 34.272653,
      "text": "The diagram now writes the equations for us. Vertically, reaction balance is weight, which is mass times gravity. 5 times 10 gives 50 Newtons. Horizontally, resultant force is tension minus friction. Tension is 22 Newtons and friction is 15 Newtons. The remaining force is 7 Newtons to the right. Force equals mass times acceleration. So the 5 kg block accelerates at 1.4 m per second squared.",
